# Godot tests — user-initiated only

Full suites take several minutes (two cold Godot startups). **Do not run them to “verify” work, before commit, or because the change touches gameplay.**

## Do not run unless the user asks

Never start these (or equivalent) on your own:

- `res://tests/run_tests.tscn`
- `res://tests/ui_smoke.tscn`
- `res://tests/screenshots.tscn`
- `playtest.bat` (repo root or `tools/playtest.bat`)
- `tools/build.sh` or any command whose main purpose is export + full test pass

Reading test code, editing `tests/`, or explaining failures from logs the user pasted is fine without running Godot.

## When the user asks to test

Treat these as explicit permission to run Godot (run only what they name):

- “run tests”, “playtest”, “run the suite”, “ui_smoke”, “run_tests”
- “verify in Godot”, “make sure tests pass”, “fix until green” **when they clearly mean execute the suites**

If they only want a code change, implement it and stop — do not add a test run “while you’re here.”

When you do run headless tests, use the Godot binary path from the **godot-path** rule and prefer `Godot_v4.7.2-stable_win64_console.exe` when it exists. See `docs/TESTING.md` for scenes and tagged subsets (e.g. balance-only slices) if the user wants something narrower than the full suite.

## If you’re unsure

Ask once: “Want me to run `run_tests`, `ui_smoke`, or both?” Do not launch Godot without an answer.
